yclopedia/archduke-rainer-joseph-of-austria"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/archduke-rainer-joseph-of-austria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archduke Rainer Joseph of Austria</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archduke Rainer Joseph was a son of Emperor Leopold II and brother of Francis I of Austria.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archelaus-i-of-macedon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/archelaus-i-of-macedon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archelaus I of Macedon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archelaus I was king of Macedon from about 413 to 399 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/archelaus-of-cappadocia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/archelaus-of-cappadocia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Archelaus of Cappadocia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archelaus was the last king of Cappadocia, installed by Mark Antony in 36 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/archermus"><span class="enc-name">Archermus</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archermus was a Greek sculptor of Chios active in the mid-sixth century BCE, from a family of sculptors that included his sons Bupalus and Athenis.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/archery"><span class="enc-name">Archery</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Archery is the use of bows to shoot arrows in hunting and warfare.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/archias-of-corinth"><span class="enc-name">Archias of Corinth</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Archias was a nobleman of the Bacchiad family of Corinth who, according to Greek traditi