p town in the province of Cádiz, Andalusia, Spain, set on a sandstone ridge above the Guadalete river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arcot"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arcot.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arcot</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Arcot is a town on the Palar river in Tamil Nadu, southern India, which became the capital of the Nawabs of the Carnatic under Mughal rule.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arctic-ocean"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arctic-ocean.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arctic Ocean</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arctic Ocean is the smallest and shallowest of the world's oceans, surrounding the North Pole and bordered by Europe, Asia and North America.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ardabil"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ardabil.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ardabil</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ardabil is a city in north-western Iran.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ardagh-county-longford"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ardagh-county-longford.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ardagh, County Longford</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ardagh is a village in County Longford, Ireland, whose church is traditionally said to have been founded by Saint Mel, a disciple of Saint Patrick, in the 5th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ardahan"><span class="enc-name">Ardahan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ardahan is a city in north-eastern Turkey, the capital of Ardahan Provin