img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arezzo"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arezzo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arezzo</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Arezzo is a city in eastern Tuscany, Italy, standing on a hill above the upper valleys of the Arno and Tiber.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/arg-of-karim-khan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/arg-of-karim-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Arg of Karim Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">The Arg of Karim Khan is a citadel in Shiraz built in the 1760s under Karim Khan Zand, the founder of the Zand Empire.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/arganthonios"><span class="enc-name">Arganthonios</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Arganthonius was a king of Tartessos in south-western Iberia, known from Herodotus, who says he reigned for 80 years and lived to 120.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/argead-dynasty"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/argead-dynasty.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Argead dynasty</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Argead dynasty ruled the Kingdom of Macedon from around the 7th century BCE until about 310 BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/argentina"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/argentina.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Argentina</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Argentina is a country in southern South America that emerged from the Spanish viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/argentine-civil-wars"><img class=