ss="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ariege-department.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ariège (department)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Ariège is a department of south-western France in the central Pyrenees, created in 1790 from the County of Foix and the Couserans, with its prefecture at Foix.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ariege-river"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ariege-river.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ariège (river)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ariège is a river of south-western France, about 163 km long, rising in the Pyrenees near the border with Andorra and flowing north past Foix and Pamiers to join…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/arikesari-ii"><span class="enc-name">Arikesari II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Arikesari II was a ruler of the Chalukyas of Vemulavada in present-day Telangana, feudatories of the Rashtrakutas.</span></a></li></ul>
